# Setting combinations (TC-219 – TC-254): set the row's chips, read the rate line, then drag the right handle to the
# left handle (1 s) and back to the end (3.2 s), reading the CTA price each time. Charges nothing: Enhance is not tapped.
# Starts: AI Video Enhance panel just opened with ve-real-000320-720p30 (Add Media album casebook-ve-real, third tile),
# panel at the top (trim strip visible), Mode Standard, whole video selected.
# Ends: panel at the top, whole video selected, the row's chips selected; then tap Enhance (`id layout_enhance`).
# Args: $1 = case ID, $2 = style chip id (chip_style_natural|sharp), $3 = fps chip id (chip_fps_30|60|120),
# $4 = resolution chip id (chip_resolution_720p|1080p|4k). Tapping an already-selected chip changes nothing.
# Coordinates measured 2026-11-18 on the SM-A5360 (1080 × 2400), 16.9.0 (2611091): the panel scroll (540 1750 → 1250)
# brings the Resolution chips above the CTA bar; the right handle at the end is grabbed at x 980, y 1158; at the 1 s minimum it sits at x 186 on 2611231 and x 416 on 2611251 (1 s minimum selection, P0087 fix; R4-g1 recalibrated).
case $1
fingerdrag 540 1750 540 1250 10
id $2
id $3
id $4
wait 1
els chip_
els tv_charge
shot $1-chips
fingerdrag 540 1250 540 1750 10
wait 1
fingerdrag 980 1158 100 1158 20
wait 1
els tv_
shot $1-1s
fingerdrag 416 1158 1060 1158 15
wait 2
els tv_
shot $1-full
